res\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b238f459e87d73808963a6425e909de6045142a8bc8eb6d4b9505f660db67022","event_uuid":"ccdd7ca8-f85a-447f-883a-ce5b8db8618a","position":{"commit_sha":"c479dfa8c97f7fbd9114142f66677402dcda36d6","position":"1787795978707772001-ccdd7ca8-f85a-447f-883a-ce5b8db8618a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7612792cc7d26d090c48c2179bec8e63afd1110cb28d060999c8096120da7f26","event_uuid":"7b8d506b-628f-4b04-942b-995351e557e3","position":{"commit_sha":"225ff7a5f69bc39a460b0665580c47338a8a5619","position":"1787796515749159001-7b8d506b-628f-4b04-942b-995351e557e3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2a327ba15ca20bb1589298041814e361d500b4f0d649c31cafc6e6e5d11e592d","event_uuid":"17d882a6-43d5-445c-adbc-030c6621faa8","position":{"commit_sha":"a1cde82ba3cc98db5072b778b60bc10162f89803","position":"1787796679852060001-17d882a6-43d5-445c-adbc-030c6621faa8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c2d635a3603b82d02fb145e5f913414028227cbf563379bdefb2f44e2c99f257","event_uuid":"1ffe5616-3e02-4389-a238-56234034f38a","position":{"commit_sha":"a1cde82ba3cc98db5072b778b60bc10162f89803","position":"1787796682599458001-1ffe5616-3e02-4389-a238-56234034f38a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-246_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"06f3f99e-d9f9-40f8-a094-ac8d1c624cfd","comments":[],"created_at":1787771609645569001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2d80a6f2-18a9-4afa-92bd-590650f778d9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7e9e-07f7-8fe1-4e38"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`7e9e-07f7-8fe1-4e38` delivered gateway correlation headers but explicitly deferred the\nrun-level root span. The consequence is stated in that epic's Out-of-scope and is real: rebar\nopens no span per gate run, so `tracing.py`'s per-candidate spans are each their own trace root.\nA plan-review that fans out across chunk, container and verify calls therefore appears in\nLangfuse as many traces rather than one, and the gateway header id (minted at the boundary when\nnothing is recording) does not match any of them.\n\nPrior-art review of the header design flagged this as the idiomatic end state — Langfuse's own\nmodel is one trace per unit of work — and the epic's own plan-review confirmed the shipped\nbehaviour does not achieve it.\n\n## Approach\n\nOpen one rebar-owned span at each gate run boundary in `workflow/gate_dispatch.py`, so every\nagent call in the run nests beneath it and the run is one trace.\n`run_identity.mint_run_identity` already prefers an active recording span's trace id over\nminting, so the correlation header and the exported spans then carry the same value with no\nfurther change — that read exists precisely to make this cheap.\n\n**The span must ENCLOSE the `gate_config(...)` statement, not sit inside it.** Both sites read\n`gate_config(with_identity(cfg, ...))` (`:174`, `:706`), and `with_identity` is evaluated as an\nARGUMENT — it runs before the `with` body opens. A span opened inside that block would therefore\nnot be the active recording span when `mint_run_identity` fires, and it would mint anyway,\nsilently defeating the whole change. This ordering is the load-bearing fact.\n\n**Three boundaries, not two.** `produce_code_review_verdict` (`:372`) is the third gate-run\nboundary, with its own multi-pass fan-out whose per-candidate spans are equally separate trace\nroots. It is IN scope: it opens no `gate_config`/`with_identity`, so it gains the one-trace-\nper-run grouping but not header correlation — which is the right outcome, since `review-code`\nhas no ticket and its `${run:...}` headers are omitted by design.\n\nContextvar propagation into the parallel fan-out already works (`generation._submit_ctx` runs\neach pool task under `copy_context()`), so no threading work is required.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — open the run span ENCLOSING all three\n  boundaries (`:174` plan-review, `:706` completion, `:372` code-review).\n- `src/rebar/llm/tracing.py` — the span factory, alongside the existing `candidate_span`.\n- `tests/unit/test_run_span.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: in-process unit tests against the real tracer — span parentage runs for real in-process.\n\n- Happy path: candidate spans opened inside a gate run share the run span's trace id.\n- Parallel path: a candidate span opened inside a `_submit_ctx`-submitted pool task shares it\n  too — the fan-out is the whole point, so a main-context-only assertion proves nothing.\n- Edge: with no tracer configured, behaviour is unchanged and nothing raises.\n- Fail-open: a configured tracer that raises on span open does not abort the run — the same\n  best-effort discipline `candidate_span` follows.\n- Correlation: `mint_run_identity` inside the run returns the run span's trace id, so the\n  gateway header and the exported spans agree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Two candidate spans opened within one gate run share a trace id; checked by asserting both\n      against the run span's context.\n- [ ] A candidate span opened INSIDE a `generation._submit_ctx` pool task shares the run span's\n      trace id; checked by submitting the span-opening work through the real `_submit_ctx` and\n      comparing. This is the load-bearing case: the criterion above passes even if both spans\n      open on the main context, leaving the parallel-propagation path — which is the entire\n      reason a fanned-out run is currently many traces — unexercised.\n- [ ] Inside a gate run with a recording tracer, `mint_run_identity` returns that run span's\n      trace id rather than a minted value — the assertion that fails if the span is opened\n      inside rather than around the `gate_config(with_identity(...))` statement.\n- [ ] A code-review run's candidate spans share one trace id; checked by asserting two of them\n      against each other, proving the third boundary is covered.\n- [ ] With no tracer configured the gate run behaves exactly as before; checked by asserting no\n      exception and an unchanged verdict shape.\n- [ ] With a tracer CONFIGURED that raises on span open, the gate run still completes with an\n      unchanged verdict shape — the failure is swallowed and logged, never propagated; checked\n      by a test whose tracer raises, mirroring the guard `candidate_span` already uses. This is\n      a new failure point whose blast radius is the whole run, and `tracing.py`'s standing rule\n      is that tracing must never break an operation.\n- [ ] `gate_dispatch.py` stays at or under the 800-line module cap.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"open the run span at both gate boundaries"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/tracing.py","reason":"the run-span factory"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_run_span.py","reason":"new tests for span parentage and identity agreement"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"17d882a6-43d5-445c-adbc-030c6621faa8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8772-d92c-5682-4718","ticket_type":"story","title":"Open a rebar-owned root span per gate run so one run is one trace","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8d5e036b-38bc-46a0-b19e-b92f2ba2bb49","2d80a6f2-18a9-4afa-92bd-590650f778d9","3d73764b-fd88-4b9e-99b8-6b450cbc9a3d","31a7e273-659c-4b3f-8475-0503cc1d2d93","1902cd6f-0522-48a2-969e-eeae3d2ca0f7","e99ca110-cbde-4309-9548-09c71b428588","ef4923dd-06c6-4d49-8de8-3b9035313efc","ccdd7ca8-f85a-447f-883a-ce5b8db8618a","7b8d506b-628f-4b04-942b-995351e557e3","17d882a6-43d5-445c-adbc-030c6621faa8","1ffe5616-3e02-4389-a238-56234034f38a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787799909576016001,"uuid":"f3af89e1-7708-4db8-875d-4bc32e6790b2"}